Cloak is a local secrets vault. Secrets are AEAD-encrypted at rest under a key derived from your
passphrase via Argon2id. Reveal is gated behind local user-presence checks.

Usage: cloak [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  setup          Interactive first-time setup (vault + daemon + MCP clients + .env)
  doctor         Read-only diagnostic. Exits 1 if any check fails
  init           Initialize a new vault (interactive passphrase + KDF autotune)
  add            Add a new secret. Prompts for the value with echo OFF
  set            Update the value of an existing secret. Prompts with echo OFF
  get            Get metadata for a secret (name / kind / tags / timestamps). Never returns
                 plaintext
  list           List secrets (metadata only). Empty vault prints "(no secrets)"
  rm             Remove secret(s). Bulk modes: `--tag T`, `--all`
  show           Reveal a secret's plaintext (user-presence gated, TTY-only)
  status         Print vault file status and daemon unlock state when available
  completions    Print shell completions
  daemon-unlock  Push the vault passphrase to the running `cloakd` so MCP peers can serve requests
                 [aliases: unlock]
  import         Import a `.env` file into the vault
  export         Export the vault to a `.env` file (user-presence gated)
  run            Run a command with vault secrets injected as environment variables
  panic          Emergency: lock the vault, kill the daemon, print rotation worksheet
  daemon         Manage the cloakd background daemon (install/start/stop/restart/status)
  claude         Register `cloak` with installed MCP clients (Claude Desktop, etc.)
  restore        Re-derive vault access from your 24-word BIP-39 recovery seed
  backup         Backup utilities: confirm the recovery seed you wrote down
  audit          Audit-log utilities
  help           Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --vault <PATH>
          Path to the vault file (default: `$DATA_DIR/cloak/vault.cloak`)

      --no-biometric
          Disable local user-presence prompts after passphrase unlock for secret materialization
          commands

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
